# ACL rules of jantrik_ingest, the device receiver's Redis user (docs/deploy.md → Redis).
# Read by deploy/redis/start-redis.sh (production compose) and apps/api/test/redis-acl.e2e-spec.ts.
# `{prefix}` stands for QUEUE_PREFIX. Lines starting with # are comments; the rest is joined.
#
# Keys: the receiver's own (ingest:refused, ingest:refused-log:<sn>, ingest:trusted:<sn>:<ip>),
# its rate-limit counters (rl:ingest-ip:, rl:ingest-refused-ip:, rl:ingest-sn:) and the devices
# queue it adds jobs to. No Pub/Sub channel.
resetkeys ~ingest:* ~rl:ingest-* ~{prefix}:devices:*
resetchannels
# Commands: reading and writing those keys, and running BullMQ's Lua scripts (EVALSHA, then EVAL
# when the script is not cached yet); then nothing dangerous
# (FLUSHALL, KEYS, CONFIG, DEBUG, SHUTDOWN, ACL...), no SCRIPT or FUNCTION management.
-@all +@read +@write +eval +evalsha
-@dangerous
# FUNCTION LOAD, FLUSH, DELETE and RESTORE are @write: never server-side code that outlives the call.
-function
# INFO is dangerous by category, but ioredis's ready check and BullMQ's version check need it.
+info
# The rate limiter and the refused-serials list write in MULTI/EXEC transactions.
+multi +exec +discard
